  "source": "EAMCET 2011 (Engineering)",
  "question": "A non-conducting body floats in a liquid at $20°$C with $\\dfrac{2}{3}$ of its volume immersed in the liquid. When the liquid temperature is increased to $100°$C, $\\dfrac{3}{4}$ of the body's volume is immersed. The coefficient of real expansion of the liquid is (neglecting the expansion of the container of the liquid)",
  "diagram": "",
  "diagram_alt": "",
  "options": [
    {
      "text": "$1.56 \\times 10^{-4}\\ °\\text{C}^{-1}$",
      "image": ""
    },
