  "answer": "B",
  "numerical_answer": "",
  "tolerance": "",
  "solution": "Floating: $f\\rho$ is constant, so $\\dfrac{\\rho_{20}}{\\rho_{100}} = \\dfrac{f_{100}}{f_{20}} = \\dfrac{3/4}{2/3} = \\dfrac{9}{8}$.\n\n$\\dfrac{\\rho_{20}}{\\rho_{100}} = 1 + \\gamma(80)$:\n$$\\gamma = \\frac{1/8}{80} = 1.56 \\times 10^{-3} = 15.6 \\times 10^{-4}\\ °\\text{C}^{-1}$$",
